{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bend type is used in guitar notation and tablature. A single note with a bend and release will contain two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bend elements: the first to represent the bend and the second to represent the release. The shape attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distinguishes between the angled bend symbols commonly used in standard notation and the curved bend symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"commonly used in both tablature and standard notation."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBend","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<bend>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"MXLBend","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLBendV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBend","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBend","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend\/init(alter:content:withBar:shape:position:font:color:sound:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend\/alter","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend\/color","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend\/content-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend\/font","d